# Enkaku — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so never put a real
# secret here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# HOW IT IS LOADED, AND THE ONE PLACE IT IS NOT
# ---------------------------------------------
# Bun loads this file automatically for anything it *runs as code* — the core, the cloud
# agent, and every script under `scripts/`. Nothing else is needed: no dotenv package, no
# import.
#
# It is NOT expanded inside `package.json` script strings. `bun run dev:studio` resolves
# `${NEXT_PUBLIC_ENKAKU_CORE_URL:-...}` in a shell that never saw this file, so a value set
# here would be silently ignored there. Studio's own variables therefore live in
# `packages/studio/.env` (Next.js loads that one itself) — see `packages/studio/.env.example`.
#
# Precedence is env > file > default (spec §5). A real shell variable always wins over this
# file, which is what makes one-off overrides work:
#
#   ENKAKU_LOG_LEVEL=debug bun run dev
#
# Everything here is optional. Plain `bun run dev` works with this file absent entirely.


# ── Core ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the database, tools, artifacts and logs live. The dev scripts already point at
# .dev-data/ .dev-cloud/ .dev-agent/, so set this only to override that.
# ENKAKU_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/enkaku

# ENKAKU_PORT=7700
# ENKAKU_BIND=127.0.0.1          # non-loopback ⇒ server auth mode ⇒ TLS required
# ENKAKU_CONFIG=<dataDir>/enkaku.config.json
# ENKAKU_MODE=orchestrator       # cloud control plane; never touches local adb
# ENKAKU_LOG_LEVEL=info          # debug | info | warn | error
# ENKAKU_LOG_JSON=1              # JSON-lines output, for shipping to a log collector
# ENKAKU_STUDIO_DIST=<cwd>/packages/studio/out


# ── Auth and TLS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auth mode is derived from the bind address unless forced here. A non-loopback bind in
# `local` mode fails the boot rather than silently exposing an unauthenticated farm.
# ENKAKU_AUTH_MODE=auto          # auto | local | server
# ENKAKU_TLS_MODE=off            # off | self | external
# ENKAKU_TLS_CERT=/path/fullchain.pem
# ENKAKU_TLS_KEY=/path/privkey.pem
# ENKAKU_ALLOW_INSECURE=1        # server mode without TLS. Testing only; it warns loudly.
# ENKAKU_PUBLISH_TOKEN=          # require a token on POST /api/scripts


# ── Device network route (the proxy feature) ───────────────────────────────────
# Without a probe endpoint the `egress`, `geo` and `dns` checks stay `skip` and a route's
# health can never rise above `unverified` — applied, but never confirmed to be carrying
# traffic. That is deliberate: an unproven route must never report itself healthy.
#
# Any endpoint that echoes the caller's address works for the `egress` check. Real DNS-leak
# detection needs one you host yourself, because it has to observe which resolver actually
# looked up the name — see docs/plans/51-m24b-verified-egress-and-fail-closed.md §3.3.
# ENKAKU_NETWORK_PROBE_URL=https://api.ipify.org/?format=json

# Sticky-session template for the upstream username, so a device keeps the same exit address
# across reconnects. Provider-specific — SOAX and others each spell it differently — so it is
# a template rather than a hardcoded format. `{id}` is the device's stable session id.
# Leave unset for no stickiness.
# ENKAKU_NETWORK_SESSION_TEMPLATE={username}-sessionid-{id}


# ── Guest agent (the on-device APK) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Resolution order: this variable, then a local Gradle build under apps/guest-agent/, then
# the sha256-pinned artifact from the Toolchain Manager. Set this only to pin a one-off
# build; a checkout that has run `bun run build:guest-agent` needs nothing.
# ENKAKU_GUEST_AGENT_PATH=$PWD/apps/guest-agent/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk


# ── Cloud mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_CP_URL=http://localhost:7700    # control plane, required for the agent
# ENKAKU_ENROLL_TOKEN=                   # one-time, first run only; discarded afterwards
# ENKAKU_AGENT_NAME=
# ENKAKU_PUBLIC_URL=


# ── WebRTC ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_STUN_URL=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302
# ENKAKU_TURN_URL=
# ENKAKU_TURN_USER=
# ENKAKU_TURN_PASSWORD=
# ENKAKU_TURN_SECRET=            # must match coturn's static-auth-secret


# ── Lease and scheduler ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_LEASE_JOB_TTL=60
# ENKAKU_LEASE_HEARTBEAT_MS=15000
# ENKAKU_LEASE_MANUAL_IDLE_TIMEOUT=300
# ENKAKU_LEASE_REAPER_MS=5000
# ENKAKU_SCHEDULER_INTERVAL_MS=2000


# ── Job isolation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Crash containment, not a security sandbox — never describe it as one (spec §11.3).
# ENKAKU_JOB_ISOLATION=process   # process | container
# ENKAKU_JOB_IMAGE=oven/bun:1
# ENKAKU_JOB_CPUS=
# ENKAKU_JOB_MEMORY_MB=
# ENKAKU_OCI_RUNTIME=            # e.g. runsc for gVisor
# ENKAKU_CONTAINER_RUNTIME=


# ── Toolchain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_TOOLS_MANIFEST_URL=
# ENKAKU_UI_SERVER_PORT_RANGE=27100-27299
# ENKAKU_ADB_PATH=               # dev/test only; logs a warning whenever it is used.
                                 # The generic form is ENKAKU_<TOOL_ID>_PATH.


# ── SDK / CLI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_FARM_URL=http://localhost:7700
# ENKAKU_TOKEN=


# ── Licensing and telemetry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_LICENSE_FILE=<dataDir>/license.json
# ENKAKU_LICENSE_PUBKEY=
# ENKAKU_TELEMETRY_URL=
# ENKAKU_FEED_URL=


# ── Tests ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tests needing a physical device are skipped unless this is set, so `bun test` stays green
# with nothing plugged in.
# ENKAKU_TEST_DEVICE=1

# Upstream for the guest-agent smoke test. Without it the route stages skip rather than fail.
# Use a scratch credential — never a production one.
# ENKAKU_SMOKE_PROXY=socks5://user:pass@host:1080
